        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.651,
            0.201,
            0.764,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "What do you observe?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.266,
            0.868,
            0.296
          ],
          "content": "• Are the lengths $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ and $\\frac { 2 } { 4 }$ equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.306,
            0.501,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.303,
            0.867,
            0.37
          ],
          "content": "• Are the lengths $\\frac { 2 } { 4 }$ and $\\frac{4}{8}$ equal? We can say that $\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{4}{8}$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.406,
            0.502,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.502,
            0.884,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": "These are ‘equivalent fractions’ that denote the same length, but they are expressed in terms of different fractional units."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.547,
            0.884,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "Now, check whether $\\frac { 1 } { 3 }$ and $\\frac{2}{6}$ are equivalent fractions or not, using paper strips."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.593,
            0.884,
            0.639
          ],
          "content": "Make your own fraction wall using such strips as given in the picture below!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.645,
            0.884,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "Answer the following questions after looking at the fraction wall:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.682,
            0.543,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "1. Are the lengths $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ and $\\frac{3}{6}$ equal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.713,
            0.461,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "2. Are $\\frac{2}{3}$ and $\\frac{4}{6}$ equivalent fractions? Why?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.775,
            0.46,
            0.863
          ],
          "content": "3. \u0007How many pieces of length $\\frac{1}{6}$ will make a length of $\\frac { 1 } { 2 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.47,
            0.711,
            0.88,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td colspan=\"12\">1 UNIT</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"6\">12</td><td colspan=\"6\">22</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"4\">13</td><td colspan=\"4\">23</td><td colspan=\"4\">33</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\">14</td><td colspan=\"3\">24</td><td colspan=\"3\">34</td><td colspan=\"3\">44</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\">15</td><td colspan=\"3\">25</td><td colspan=\"2\">35</td><td colspan=\"3\">45</td><td colspan=\"2\">55</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td colspan=\"3\">26</td><td colspan=\"2\">36</td><td colspan=\"2\">46</td><td colspan=\"3\">56</td><td>66</td></tr></tbody></table>",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_table_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.881,
            0.785,
